i\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[46,36],"translations":{"de":["Multidisziplin\u00e4r","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Multidisciplinary","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Multidisciplinare","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Pluridisciplinaire","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Multidisciplinar","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Multidisciplinair","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Something Beautiful","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"pt":{"name":"Something Beautiful","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"en":{"name":"Something Beautiful Festival","shortdescr":"The Something Beautiful Festival is a multidisciplinary, multilingual celebration of the visual arts and poetry, bringing together diverse talents and fostering an immersive, participatory experience with the public. During the festival, artists and participants embark on a profound and sensitive exploration of time, movement, our environment and the human gesture and body.","longdescr":"The Something Beautiful festival brings together poetry and a variety of other artistic languages, both visual and linguistic, showcasing  diverse talents and encouraging a participative experience with the public.\n\nThe festival is a multidisciplinary, multilingual celebration of the visual arts and poetry. The programme includes a major group exhibition - curated by the festival organisers - performances, readings, open stages, and workshops for all ages.\n\nThe public will encounter a number of names from the Belgian and international contemporary art scene, such as Haleh Chinikar, Marianne Csaky, Nina De Angelis, Laure For\u00eat, Aur\u00e9lie Gravelat,Miriam Rose Gronwald, Marion Guillard, Marion Henry, Gabrielle Herv\u00e9, Kiran Katara, Mimi Kunz, St\u00e9fan Tul\u00e9po, and many others.\n\nThere will also be collaborations with various artistic groups, such as the Singing Molenbeek choir, which will open the festival, and different poetry circles, such as the International Poetry Caf\u00e9.\n \nSomething Beautiful is designed for the people living in Brussels who are interested in art and\/or poetry, and especially for the residents of Molenbeek. The festival seeks to create a common space through artistic language, with the aim of enriching the local artistic landscape and highlighting Molenbeek as a plural and open commune. Something Beautiful works with a network of committed local partners to encourage encounters between the public and the sensitive and political experience of art.\n\nThe festival is multilingual, which adds another  layer  to the artistic experience: several languages will be present and supported. Participants will have the opportunity, at different times, to express themselves in the language that inspires them most and to share their artistic creations.\n\nThe festival is free (with the exception of the banquet po\u00e9tique), and the activities are based on three key principles: active discovery of artistic practices, through a range of creative workshops for children, young people and adults; the sharing of experiences in the form of open stages, where the public can express themselves freely and exchange ideas through art; and the encounter, through guided tours to enable the public to explore the exhibitions in an interactive way and discuss the dynamics of creation.\n\nLaVall\u00e9e is accessible to people with reduced mobility, with the exception of the corridor floor accessible only by stairs. ","performers":"Haleh Chinikar, Marianne Csaky, Nina De Angelis, Laure For\u00eat, Aur\u00e9lie Gravelat, Miriam Rose Gronwald, Marion Guillard, Marion Henry, Gabrielle Herveet, Kiran Katara, Mimi Kunz, St\u00e9fan Tul\u00e9po, Maria Komarova, Congago, Singularity A.I., ILL SYLL, Hanna Ilczyszyn, Chantal Purcell O\u2019Byrne, Sofie Verraest, Paul Stephenson, Sarah Reader Harris, Marieke Slovin-Lewis, Lucie Pinier, Nathalie Vanderlinden.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"it":{"name":"Something Beautiful","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"cn":{"name":"Something Beautiful","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"fr":{"name":"Something Beautiful Festival","shortdescr":"Le festival Something Beautiful est une c\u00e9l\u00e9bration pluridisciplinaire et multilingue des arts visuels et de la po\u00e9sie, r\u00e9unissant des talents divers et favorisant une exp\u00e9rience immersive et participative avec le public. Au sein du festival, les artistes et participant.es se lancent dans une exploration profonde et sensible du temps, du mouvement, de l'environnement, du geste et du corps humain.","longdescr":"Le festival Something Beautiful promeut la rencontre entre la po\u00e9sie et d'autres langages artistiques vari\u00e9s, qu'ils soient plastiques ou linguistiques, en r\u00e9unissant des talents divers et en privil\u00e9giant une exp\u00e9rience collaborative avec le public.\n \nLe festival est une c\u00e9l\u00e9bration pluridisciplinaire et multilingue des arts visuels et de la po\u00e9sie. Le programme comprend une grande exposition collective \u2013 guid\u00e9e par les organisatrices du festival - , des performances, des lectures, des sc\u00e8nes ouvertes et des ateliers pour les petits et pour les grands.\n \nLe public pourra retrouver plusieurs noms de la sc\u00e8ne contemporaine belge et internationale, tels que Haleh Chinikar, Marianne Csaky, Nina De Angelis, Laure For\u00eat, Aur\u00e9lie Gravelat,Miriam Rose Gronwald, Marion Guillard, Marion Henry, Gabrielle Herv\u00e9, Kiran Katara, Mimi Kunz, St\u00e9fan Tul\u00e9po, et bien d\u2019autres. \n\nIl y aura \u00e9galement des collaborations avec diff\u00e9rents collectifs artistiques, comme la chorale Singing Molenbeek, qui ouvrira le festival, et diff\u00e9rents cercles de po\u00e9sie, comme l'International Poetry Caf\u00e9.\n\nSomething Beautiful s\u2019adresse aux habitant.e.s de Bruxellois.e.s int\u00e9ress\u00e9.e.s par l\u2019art et\/ou la po\u00e9sie, et particuli\u00e8rement  aux habitant.e.s de Molenbeek . Le festival cherche \u00e0 cr\u00e9er un espace commun par le biais du langage artistique, visant \u00e0 enrichir le paysage artistique local ainsi qu\u2019\u00e0 mettre en valeur Molenbeek, une commune plurielle et ouverte. Something Beautiful collabore avec un r\u00e9seau de partenaires locaux et engag\u00e9s sur le terrain afin de permettre une rencontre entre le public et l\u2019exp\u00e9rience sensible et politique de l\u2019art.\n \nLe festival est essentiellement multilingue, ce qui ajoute une dimension suppl\u00e9mentaire \u00e0 l\u2019exp\u00e9rience artistique : plusieurs langues seront pr\u00e9sentes et encourag\u00e9es, les participant.es auront l'opportunit\u00e9, \u00e0 diff\u00e9rents moments, de s'exprimer dans la langue qui les inspire les plus afin de  partager leurs cr\u00e9ations artistiques. \n \nLe festival est gratuit (sauf le banquet po\u00e9tique) et les activit\u00e9s s'appuient sur trois principes essentiels : la d\u00e9couverte active d'une pratique technique et artistique \u00e0 travers diff\u00e9rents ateliers cr\u00e9atifs pour les enfants, les jeunes et les adultes ; le partage sous forme de sc\u00e8nes ouvertes, o\u00f9 le public peut s'exprimer librement et \u00e9changer par le biais de l\u2019art ; et la rencontre, \u00e0 travers des visites guid\u00e9es afin de permettre au public de parcourir les expositions de mani\u00e8re interactive et de discuter de la dynamique de la cr\u00e9ation.\n \nLes espaces de LaVall\u00e9e sont accessibles aux personnes \u00e0 mobilit\u00e9 r\u00e9duite, \u00e0 l'exception de l'\u00e9tage des coursives o\u00f9 l'acc\u00e8s se fait uniquement par des escaliers.","performers":"Haleh Chinikar, Marianne Csaky, Nina De Angelis, Laure For\u00eat, Aur\u00e9lie Gravelat, Miriam Rose Gronwald, Marion Guillard, Marion Henry, Gabrielle Herveet, Kiran Katara, Mimi Kunz, St\u00e9fan Tul\u00e9po, Maria Komarova, Congago, Singularity A.I., ILL SYLL, Hanna Ilczyszyn, Chantal Purcell O\u2019Byrne, Sofie Verraest, Paul Stephenson, Sarah Reader Harris, Marieke Slovin-Lewis, Lucie Pinier, Nathalie Vanderlinden.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"sp":{"name":"Something Beautiful","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/somethingbeautiful.be","email":"annasnog@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50002643"},"nl":{"name":"Something Beautiful Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":"Haleh Chinikar, Marianne Csaky, Nina De Angelis, Laure For\u00eat, Aur\u00e9lie Gravelat, Miriam Rose Gr