null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.muntpunt.be","email":"info@muntpunt.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 278 11 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.563554"},"nl":{"name":"Black Voices Podcast Festival | Live Sessions (EN)","shortdescr":"Discover today's best podcasts centering black creators and storytellers from Belgium and beyond.","longdescr":"The Black Voices Podcast Festival by Som\u2022m\u2022e Of Us aims to shine a light on the contributions of Belgium-based black creators in the world of independent podcasting, who are still too often underrepresented and under celebrated.\n\nThe goal of this event is to bring people from local black communities together through live recordings with an audience and via inspiring and insightful workshops.\n\nAs for each Som\u2022m\u2022e Of Us project, the Black Voices Podcast Festival will ultimately contribute to the building of an archive of Black cultural creations located and germinating in Belgium. The Black Voices Podcast Festival will offer five days of live podcast recordings curated by the Som\u2022m\u2022e of Us collective.\n\nProgram:\n\n- 25\/10\u00a0| 20:00 - 21:30 | Reclaiming Our Joy: Sarah Diedro Jord\u00e3o\n- 26\/10\u00a0| 20:00 - 21:30 |\u00a0What's Up With Reine?\u00a0x Menji Talks\n- 27\/10 | 20:00 - 21:30 | The Aftertea Podcast: Sonia Dorcas Mutaganzwa, Fouzia Sadala & Marck Kapenda + afterparty (TBC)\n- 28\/10 | 15:00 - 18:00 | Workshop - DIY podcasting with Sonia Dorcas (The Aftertea Podcast)\n\nSom\u2022m\u2022e Of Us is a multidisciplinarycollective of independent black cultural curators and community space organizers.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.muntpunt.be","email":"info@muntpunt.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 278 11 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.563554"}},"place":{"id":277273,"translations":