ages":{"spoken":["nl","en","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibition","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[37,36],"translations":{"de":["Audiovisuelle K\u00fcnste","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Audiovisual art","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Arti audiovisive","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Arts audiovisuels","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Artes audiovisuales","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Audiovisuele kunst","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Digital Devotion","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"pt":{"name":"Digital Devotion","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"en":{"name":"Connecting","shortdescr":"Technology is omnipresent in our daily lives, but what do our online relationships actually represent? How do we inhabit a community through an app? What does it mean to be friends through platforms and avatars? And is there room for love in the metaverse? \"Connecting\" traces the links between physical reality and the digital world.","longdescr":"Until recently, digital tools were nothing more than translations of physical applications: mail became e-mail, shopping increasingly happened online, banks funneled people to their apps. Then Web 2.0 and social media gradually changed the spaces where we interact. However the transformation did not end there and the boundaries between digital and physical worlds continued to blur. Today we converse on ChatGPT, draw up contracts via blockchain technology, and play games in boundless virtual universes.\n\n \n\nThe digital world keeps building where the physical world ends. Living and non-living entities become interconnected, much like in animistic belief systems and cosmologies where non-human forms like rivers, mountains, animals, and stones have long been revered for their vitality and potential. Emotion, intimacy, and attention are no longer inherently human qualities. This obscuration of what it means to be alive generates a form of worldbuilding that surpasses human limitations.\n\n \n\nConnecting imagines new interdependencies between humans and non-humans. These connections expand and reshape our understanding of affection, kinship, and relationships. In investigating this new texture of experience, artists in the exhibition reflect on the transformative quality of technology in shaping our emotional worlds.\n\n \n\nArtists: Korakrit Arunanondchai & Alex Gvojic, Zach Blas, Ian Cheng, Keiken, Eva L\u2019Hoest, Tabita Rezaire and Natasha Tontey.\n\nThe work by Keiken is co-commissioned by KANAL and the Helsinki Biennale.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"it":{"name":"Digital Devotion","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"cn":{"name":"Digital Devotion","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"fr":{"name":"Connecting","shortdescr":"La technologie est partout dans notre quotidien. Mais que repr\u00e9sentent nos relations en ligne? Peut-on faire communaut\u00e9 par le biais d\u2019une application? Quel sens donner \u00e0 l\u2019amiti\u00e9 qui se forme \u00e0 travers les plateformes et les avatars? Trouve-t-on l\u2019amour dans le m\u00e9tavers? \"Connecting\" trace les liens entre la r\u00e9alit\u00e9 physique et le monde num\u00e9rique. ","longdescr":"Il y a quelques ann\u00e9es, les outils num\u00e9riques ne faisaient que traduire en ligne des services physiques: le courrier s\u2019est transform\u00e9 en courriel, les achats se sont d\u00e9plac\u00e9s en ligne, les banques ont redirig\u00e9 leurs clients vers des applications. Ensuite, le Web 2.0 et les m\u00e9dias sociaux ont petit \u00e0 petit chang\u00e9 les espaces de nos interactions. Et la transformation ne s\u2019est pas arr\u00eat\u00e9e l\u00e0: les fronti\u00e8res entre le monde num\u00e9rique et le monde physique n\u2019ont cess\u00e9 de s\u2019estomper. Aujourd\u2019hui, en plus de discuter avec ChatGPT ou de signer des contrats via la technologie blockchain, nos jeux virtuels nous embarquent dans des mondes autog\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9s \u00e0 l\u2019infini.\n\nLe monde num\u00e9rique continue sa construction l\u00e0 o\u00f9 le monde physique s\u2019arr\u00eate. Les entit\u00e9s humaines et non-humaines s\u2019y interconnectent, \u00e0 l\u2019image des cosmologies animistes qui reconnaissent depuis longtemps la vivacit\u00e9 et le potentiel des rivi\u00e8res, des montagnes, des animaux et des pierres. Les \u00e9motions, l\u2019intimit\u00e9 et l\u2019attention ne sont plus consid\u00e9r\u00e9es comme des caract\u00e9ristiques fondamentalement humaines. Que signifie aujourd\u2019hui \u00eatre vivant? Cette question est \u00e0 la base de la construction de mondes qui d\u00e9passent les limitations humaines.\n\n\"Connecting\" imagine de nouvelles interd\u00e9pendances entre les humains et les non-humains. Ces connexions \u00e9tendent et fa\u00e7onnent notre compr\u00e9hension de l\u2019affect, des liens d\u2019appartenance et des relations. En explorant la texture nouvelle de ces exp\u00e9riences, les artistes de l\u2019exposition s\u2019int\u00e9ressent au pouvoir de transformation que la technologie a sur nos univers \u00e9motionnels.\n\n\nArtistes:  Korakrit Arunanondchai & Alex Gvojic, Zach Blas, Ian Cheng, Keiken, Eva L\u2019Hoest, Tabita Rezaire et Natasha Tontey.\n\nL\u2019oeuvre du collectif londonien Keiken est commissionn\u00e9e par KANAL-Centre Pompidou et la biennale d\u2019Helsinki.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"sp":{"name":"Digital Devotion","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"},"nl":{"name":"Connecting","shortdescr":"Technologie is omnipresent in ons dagelijks leven. Maar wat betekenen onze online relaties? Hoe leven we in gemeenschap via de app? Wat betekent vriendschap via platformen en avatars? En is er plaats voor liefde in de metaverse? \"Connecting\" linkt de fysieke realiteit aan de digitale wereld. ","longdescr":"Digitale tools waren tot voor kort niets meer dan vertalingen van fysieke toepassingen: mail werd e-mail, shoppen ging steeds vaker online, bankieren doen we steevast via de bankapp. Web 2.0 en social media veranderden geleidelijk de ruimte waarin we interageren. Maar daar hield de transformatie niet op en de grenzen tussen digitale en fysieke wereld vervaagden verder. Vandaag praten we met ChatGPT, stellen we contracten op via blockchaintechnologie en gamen we in virtuele universums zonder grenzen.\n \nDe digitale wereld bouwt verder waar de fysieke eindigt. Levende en niet-levende entiteiten raken verbonden, net als bij animistische geloofssystemen en kosmologie\u00ebn, die het potentieel en de energie van het niet-menselijke \u2013 rivieren, bergen, dieren en stenen \u2013 al lange tijd onderkennen. Emotie, intimiteit en aandacht zijn niet langer uitsluitend menselijke eigenschappen. Het antwoord op de vraag wat het betekent om te leven wordt minder eenduidig en impliceert het bouwen aan een wereld die de menselijke limieten overstijgt.\n\n\"Connecting\" verbeeldt nieuwe vormen van afhankelijkheid tussen mensen en niet-mensen. Die connecties breiden uit en vervormen ons idee van affectie, verwantschap en relaties. De kunstenaars in de tentoonstelling gaan op zoek naar die nieuwe dimensies en reflecteren over de transformatieve kracht van technologie in het vormgeven van onze emotionele werelden.\n\n\nMet werken van Korakrit Arunanondchai & Alex Gvojic, Zach Blas, Ian Cheng, Keiken, Eva L\u2019Hoest, Tabita Rezaire en Natasha Tontey. Het kunstwerk van het Londense collectief Keiken werd gemaakt in opdracht van KANAL-Centre Pompidou en de Bi\u00ebnnale van Helsinki.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/kanal.brussels\/fr\/evenements\/exposition\/digital-devotion","email":"info@kanal.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 435 13 68","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555134"}},"place":{"id":279208,"translations":{"de":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"Kanal","virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Avenue du Port","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue du Port, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"K1 (KANAL-Centre Pompidou)","address_street_name":"Havenlaan","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Havenlaan, 1","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[8],"translations":{"de":["Kanal-Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["Canal"],"it":["Canal"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Canal"],"sp":["Canal"],"nl":["Kanaalwijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[20],"translations":{"de":["Norden"],"pt":[null],"en":["North"],"it":["Nord"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Nord"],"sp":["Norte"],"nl":["Noord"]}},"neca":"art_center","facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":39208,"location":{"lat":50.86046358,"lon":4.34704083},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2023-07-24T17:32:12+02:00","published_at":"2022-08-18T15:57:35+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":271094,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou       ","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Weder auf dem Gebiet der modernen und zeitgen\u00f6ssischen Kunst noch im Bereich der Architektur ist Br\u00fcssel ein unbeschriebenes Blatt. Im Gegenteil, es gibt bereits eine ganze Reihe von Museen und Einrichtungen, die sich mit den verschiedenen k\u00fcnstlerischen Disziplinen besch\u00e4ftigen. \r\nWas jedoch bislang noch fehlte, war ein Museum f\u00fcr moderne und zeitgen\u00f6ssische Kunst und ein Architekturmuseum unter einem Dach (und was f\u00fcr einem Dach!). Und so hat das ambitionierte Projekt KANAL Centre Pompidou seine absolute Daseinsberechtigung am Br\u00fcsseler Kanal, wo es die 35 000 m\u00b2 der ehemaligen Citro\u00ebn-Werkstatt in Beschlag nehmen wird. In der Zeit bis zum Beginn der Umbauarbeiten, deren Ende f\u00fcr 2022\/2023 geplant sind, hat die Fondation Kanal beschlossen, ab dem 5. Mai 2018 eine Art \"Vorlaufjahr\" zu starten. 13 Monate lang kann das Publikum in Zusammenarbeit mit dem Centre Pompidou dieses mythische Geb\u00e4ude entdecken - Ausstellungen, Gro\u00dfinstallationen, zehn Auftragsarbeiten von Br\u00fcsseler K\u00fcnstlern sowie ein Programm mit Live-Darbietungen. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou      ","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"When it reopens in 2024, Kanal-Centre Pompidou will become the largest cultural institution in Brussels, with more than 35,000m\u00b2 dedicated to current artistic creation in all its forms. After presenting KANAL BRUT - an exhibition in its own, raw space - and then a major two-part exhibition by Swiss artist John M Armleder, the huge garage closed its doors for renovation. However, Kanal remains active in the Brussels cultural sector and is multiplying its collaborations with local actors. Exhibitions and events are planned at K1, a space opposite the building site. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou      ","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou      ","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Lors de sa re\u0301ouverture pre\u0301vue en 2024, Kanal-Centre Pompidou deviendra la plus vaste institution culturelle bruxelloise, avec plus de 35.000 m\u00b2 de\u0301die\u0301s a\u0300 la cre\u0301ation artistique actuelle sous toutes ses formes. Apr\u00e8s avoir pr\u00e9sent\u00e9 \u00ab\u202fKANAL BRUT\u202f\u00bb, une exposition dans son espace encore dans son jus, puis une grande exposition en deux volets de l\u2019artiste suisse John M Armleder, l\u2019immense garage a ferm\u00e9 ses portes pour cause de travaux. Kanal reste cependant actif dans le secteur culturel \u00e0 Bruxelles et multiplie ses collaborations avec les acteurs locaux. Des expositions et des \u00e9v\u00e8nements sont notamment pr\u00e9vus au K1, un local faisant face au chantier. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou","address_street_name":"Square Sainctelette ","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Square Sainctelette ","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Kanal - Centre Pompidou","address_street_name":"Sainctelettesquare","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kanal.brussels","website":"http:\/\/www.kanal.brussels","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Sainctelettesquare","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Wanneer Kanal-Centre Pompidou in 2024 heropent, zal het de grootste culturele instelling in Brussel zijn, met meer dan 35.000 vierkante meter gewijd aan hedendaagse artistieke creatie in al haar vormen. Na de presentatie van \u2018KANAL BRUT,\u2019 een tentoonstelling in de oorspronkelijke ruimte, gevolgd door een grote tweedelige tentoonstelling van de Zwitserse kunstenaar John M. Armleder, sloot de enorme garage haar deuren voor renovatie. Kanal blijft echter actief in de culturele sector in Brussel en intensiveert zijn samenwerking met lokale spelers. Zo zijn er tentoonstellingen en evenementen gepland in K1, een ruimte net tegenover de bouwwerf.  ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"KANAL - CENTRE POMPIDOU","virtual_visit":null}},"neca":"art_center","facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":31094,"location":{"lat":50.85867303,"lon":4.3479144},"last_updated_at":"2022-10-10T10:25:09+02:00","published_at":"2018-03-21T14:36:53+01:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/b23c4ec50d441c7281f2cfdaebda14cf0403cbed.jpeg","width":1000,"height":563,"ratio":1