nsaert-Canal","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be\/fr\/visites\/les-galeries-downtown-dansaert-canal","email":"info@arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555459"},"nl":{"name":"Les galeries downtown : Dansaert-Canal","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be\/fr\/visites\/les-galeries-downtown-dansaert-canal","email":"info@arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.555459"}},"place":{"id":212483,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Occupying an impressive Art Nouveau building designed by the architect Louis Bral and then restored by architects Hilde Daem and Robbrecht, the gallery was founded in 1988 under the name of Gallery Meert Rihoux. In 2006, it changed direction and assumed the name of the new director, Greta Meert. From the start, the gallery has placed the emphasis on the minimal and conceptual art of the seventies (Donald Judd, Robert Mangold, Richard Tuttle, Robert Barry, Hanne Darboven, Niele Toroni) and also paid particular attention to photography from the eighties (Thomas Struth, Louise Lawler, Jeff Wall, Ken Lum, Ian Wallace and John Baldessari. In addition, the gallery presents a more future-focused selection of artists including Eric Baudelaire, I\u00f1aki Bonillas, Johannes Esper, Valerie Krause, Anne Neukamp, Tobias Putrih and Johannes Wald and the Belgian artists Edith Dekyndt, Stef Driesen, Sophie Nys, Koen van den Broek, Catharina van Eetvelde and Pieter Vermeersch.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"MEERT","virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Situ\u00e9e dans un magnifique immeuble art nouveau dessin\u00e9 par l\u2019architecte Louis Bral et restaur\u00e9 ensuite par les architectes Hilde Daem et Paul Robbrecht, la galerie f\u00fbt fond\u00e9e en 1988 sous le nom de Galerie Meert Rihoux. En 2006, elle change de direction et prend le nom de la nouvelle directrice, Greta Meert. D\u00e8s le d\u00e9but, la galerie met l\u2019accent sur, l\u2019art minimal et conceptuel des ann\u00e9es 70 (Donald Judd, Robert Mangold, Richard Tuttle, Robert Barry, Hanne Darboven, Niele Toroni) et porte \u00e9galement une attention particuli\u00e8re \u00e0 la photographie d'origine des ann\u00e9es 80 (Thomas Struth, Louise Lawler, Jeff Wall, Ken Lum, Ian Wallace et John Baldessari. La galerie propose par ailleurs une s\u00e9lection d\u2019artistes plus prospective comprenant une nouvelle g\u00e9n\u00e9ration de plasticiens tels que Eric Baudelaire, I\u00f1aki Bonillas, Johannes Esper, Valerie Krause, Anne Neukamp, Tobias Putrih et Johannes Wald et les Belges Edith Dekyndt, Stef Driesen, Sophie Nys, Koen van den Broek, Catharina van Eetvelde et Pieter Vermeersch.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"MEERT","virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Rue du Canal","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Canal, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Greta Meert","address_street_name":"Vaartstraat","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@galeriegretameert.com","website":"http:\/\/www.galeriegretameert.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 14 22","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Vaartstraat, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Deze galerij (opgericht in 1988 als Galerie Meert Rihoux) is gevestigd in een schitterend art-nouveaupand, getekend door architect Louis Bral en later gerestaureerd door architecten Hilde Daem en Paul Robbrecht. In 2006 nam een nieuwe directie het over en wijzigde de naam tot die van de nieuwe directrice, Greta Meert. De galerie had vanaf de start vooral oog voor het minimalisme en de conceptuele kunst van de jaren 70 (Donald Judd, Robert Mangold, Richard Tuttle, Robert Barry, Hanne Darboven, Niele Toroni). Bijzondere aandacht is er ook voor originele fotografie van de jaren 80 (Thomas Struth, Louise Lawler, Jeff Wall, Ken Lum, Ian Wallace en John Baldessari. De galerij biedt overigens een prospectieve artiestenselectie met een nieuwe generatie plastische kunstenaars zoals Eric Baudelaire, I\u00f1aki Bonillas, Johannes Esper, Valerie Krause, Anne Neukamp, Tobias Putrih en Johannes Wald en de  Belgische Edith Dekyndt, Stef Driesen, Sophie Nys, Koen van den Broek, Catharina van Eetvelde en Pieter Vermeersch.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":"MEERT","virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[3],"translations":{"de":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"pt":[null],"en":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"it":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"sp":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"nl":["Dansaertwijk\/Sint-Katelijne"]}},